1
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and
even my shoe goes flying.

3
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:42,340
onto the head of the
carpenter I was messing with.

4
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I lose my spirit somewhere else,
there's no point in it.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,540
Yawning once more, the unchanging
streets feel strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:10,440
From the pointed hat of the water tower,

8
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset sinks into the vast sky.

9
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow, too,
somehow comes to an end, doesn't it.

10
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

11
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
Only after losing it did I realize,

12
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,860
because I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,260
The way one lives

14
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,660
Whoa, what do I do?

15
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,480
What's wrong?

16
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:49,860
This is it.

17
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:51,800
Miss Honey's Love Fortunes

18
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,180
Yes, horoscopes, astrology!

19
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:57,800
It says my love luck is soaring this month!

20
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,980
Women sure love fortune-telling

21
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:01,360
Hey, Nakagawa.

22
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:06,160
The fortune teller near the
station is always packed with women.

23
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:11,660
Now that you mention it,
we don't see many men lining up.

24
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:16,960
Of course not. If a bunch of sweaty, scruffy men lined up,
people would mistake it for a betting window.

25
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:23,120
But I hear even physicists like Newton
and Einstein took fortune-telling seriously.

26
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:29,980
Everyone wants to ask someone or lean on something when they have to make an important decision,
don't they?

27
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,780
But parents often come to consult us,
don't they?

28
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:38,440
But people who come for advice have
usually already reached their own conclusion.

29
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,100
What do you mean?

30
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,260
Deep down, they've already
decided what they want to do,

31
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:47,100
but they lack the courage to take that first step,
and they're stuck.

32
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:47,660
I see.

33
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:52,680
So they just want someone they
trust to give them a little push.

34
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:57,040
Men come to me for advice all the time, too.

35
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,820
But in Ryo-san's case...

36
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:03,700
When someone has already mostly
decided which path to take,

37
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:07,760
they just drag them into a free consultation,
don't they?

38
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,920
The ones who really suffer are the
people who do exactly what Ryo-san says.

39
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:16,420
Thanks to you, Senpai,
many people have taken the wrong path.

40
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:19,900
With Ryo-chan,
even when it's the same kind of push,

41
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,120
it's just a push from one side, isn't it?

42
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:27,240
Ryo-chan, you might end up being sued
by a victims' group one of these days.

43
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:36,240
It's your own life, so decide for yourself! That's only natural.
It's the people who rely on others who are to blame.

44
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:45,860
You can handle everything yourself, can't you?
And without any hesitation before acting, you can make the most reckless choice imaginable.

45
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:54,740
Senpai thinks in digital terms, doesn't he?
Life's all or nothing: one or zero, do or die, yes or no.

46
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,060
It's one or the other, isn't it?

47
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:58,260
Hesitating is just a waste of time.

48
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:02,780
Nothing complicated or subtle
ever happens in Ryo-chan's life.

49
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:03,820
That's true.

50
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:07,240
Ryo-san's daily life really is like a caveman's,
isn't it?

51
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:10,580
Senpai really does only need yes or no,
doesn't he?

52
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,900
Don't treat me like some simple-minded fool.

53
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:21,680
I've had moments of indecision too,
you know.

54
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:25,260
At one shop, a Densuke doll
was being sold for 50,000 yen.

55
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:29,320
At 10,000 yen,
I'd have bought it without a second thought.

56
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:33,120
But 50,000 yen is such an awkward amount.

57
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:37,860
Back then I was drowning in debt
and living on 10,000 yen a month.

58
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:41,580
50,000 yen is five months'
worth of living expenses.

59
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:42,800
I agonized over it.

60
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,520
There's no room for agonizing, is there?

61
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,300
Normal people wouldn't buy it, though.

62
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:50,360
Back then I couldn't focus on work,
and I lost 10 kilos.

63
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:26,140
Sold for three times the original price? What are you talking about?
That was a different Densuke story, you know.

64
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:31,800
So that's how it is. In the end, Ryo-san only
agonizes when it comes to weighing gains and losses.

65
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:39,380
When ordinary people reach a crossroads in life,
love or courage pushes them to take the next step,

66
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:47,400
but when you hesitate, greed wins
out and that's what pushes you forward.

67
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,060
So greed is what pushes you.

68
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:51,440
Everyone has greed, you know.

69
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:52,860
Sure, but...

70
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:57,760
Ordinary people keep it in
check with reason or self-control.

71
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:01,500
But in your case,
the push of desire is far too strong.

72
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,680
It's impossible for you
to control your greed.

73
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,500
I see.

74
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,340
That might actually help.

75
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,680
Hey, look.

76
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:16,380
Isn't this the same as
what Ryo-chan is thinking?

77
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:21,060
My motto is, as long as I'm having fun now,
that's all that matters.

78
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:22,300
What I want is money.

79
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:25,240
In the future,
I want to live easily without working.

80
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,480
I see, it's just like the senior officer.

81
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:30,320
See? Young people are the same, aren't they?

82
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:35,400
Even if you're torn all year round, one word like
"limited" and you just can't help buying it.

83
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:38,880
Acting out of greed is no
different from either one.

84
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,920
In that sense, maybe the times have
finally caught up with you, senior.

85
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:43,560
Right?

86
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:50,400
But in your case, besides limited editions,
there's premium value, rarity, making money, and so on.

87
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,980
There are plenty of other landmines too,
you know.

88
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:02,760
Reiko, even you, when you hesitate over shopping,
greed pushes you, right?

89
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,400
I don't hesitate, though.

90
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:09,380
For example, if you have to pick a pet dog,
you'd choose the cutest one, wouldn't you?

91
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:13,580
Well, I'm a humanitarian,
so I'd buy them all.

92
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:17,240
Ryotsu, if you hesitate,
greed pushes you, right?

93
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,280
If I hesitate, I just don't buy.

94
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,400
Nakagawa, what about you?

95
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:24,720
I leave all my shopping to my secretary.

96
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:30,000
For example, when a company makes a 200 billion yen purchase,
you'd naturally choose whichever makes more money, right?

97
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,120
That's only natural for a president and a company,
isn't it?

98
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:37,240
No, I choose what's better for
the global environment over money.

99
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,860
The global environment?

100
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,140
Ryo-chan, are you okay?

101
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:44,940
Alright, I get it.
You two are rich and admirable people.

102
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,620
I'm just a man who only
moves for greed anyway.

103
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,860
Don't look down on poor folks, you two.

104
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,700
Pi, pi, pi, pi, pi.

105
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:54,160
We never said anything about poor people.

106
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:58,320
Shut up. Who asked you to analyze me?
Mind your own business.

107
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,721
Pushed around by greed,

108
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:03,196
you should change your ways of
living only for the present moment,

109
00:08:03,246 --> 00:08:04,080
Ryo-san.

110
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:07,400
Shut up! I'll decide my own life!

111
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,220
*Beep beep beep beep beep beep*

112
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:11,580
Take this, and more!

113
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:13,500
*Beep beep beep beep beep*

114
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,560
Senpai.

115
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,940
*Beep beep beep beep beep beep*

116
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:21,400
You're in a good mood, Ryotsu.

117
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,780
Chief, well

118
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:27,500
These two keep nagging me
about how I live my life.

119
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:28,622
Life is full of variety,

120
00:08:28,672 --> 00:08:31,520
so everyone's life plan is their own,
isn't it?

121
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:34,700
You have a life plan? Since when?

122
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,980
I'd really like to hear it.

123
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:39,580
Just the rough outline.

124
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,020
Idiot!

125
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:47,140
Normally, a person sets life goals
and lays down their own tracks,

126
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:50,580
but you're like a toy car that
just bumps into things and turns.

127
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:54,720
At your age, you still have no idea
which direction you're headed, do you?

128
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:57,140
Such rude remarks

129
00:08:57,140 --> 00:09:01,700
You just roll along with whatever is easiest,
letting things drift wherever they go.

130
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:04,180
What life plan? Idiot!

131
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:07,860
So for you, senior, the Chief is the
stopper that takes the place of your reason.

132
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:08,880
That's true.

133
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:15,720
Ryo-san, put down a bet on number 8.
Aren't you going to buy it?

134
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:19,460
I've given up on that kind of greedy,
reckless betting.

135
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:23,400
From now on, I'll bet smartly,
like an English gentleman.

136
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,440
Hmph.

137
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,160
Can you really bet on horses on greed alone?

138
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:28,980
You two don't know anything about romance.

139
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:31,136
But number 8,

140
00:09:31,186 --> 00:09:33,680
when it comes in, it really pays out big!

141
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,360
Aaaaaah!

142
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:43,900
It'd be a waste to cut number 8

143
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:49,820
Aaaaaah! What's the matter with you? Yeah,
I'm definitely buying number 8 after all!

144
00:09:50,230 --> 00:09:57,180
Number 8 to win, and a box from 8.
Yeah, go buy it for me, I'm counting on you!

145
00:09:58,460 --> 00:09:59,700
It's a guaranteed win!

146
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:11,340
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

147
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,680
He's holding the lead
all the way to the win!

148
00:10:14,020 --> 00:10:15,080
We did it!

149
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,360
Ryo-san, we did it!

150
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:18,020
We're nearly at half a million!

151
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,440
Hehehehe

152
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,221
Ryo-san,

153
00:10:20,271 --> 00:10:23,460
Tani Hayate in the next race is strong,
but for some reason nobody's betting on him.

154
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:26,200
If he comes in, the payout'll be massive.

155
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:28,940
Nah, this time I'll play it
safe and bet on a horse I like.

156
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:33,400
But long shots really
do pay big when they hit.

157
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,000
This is all thanks to greed.

158
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,660
Ugh, whoa!

159
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:37,820
What's wrong, Ryo-san?

160
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,400
Are you okay?

161
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:44,140
Whoa! Sis, where are you going?

162
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:47,740
Ugh... ugh... ugh... damn it!
I won't lose to greed!

163
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,260
Whoa!

164
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:54,840
Y-yeah, I... I won't... okay, I won't lose!

165
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,260
Whoa! Damn it!

166
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,180
Which one is it?

167
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:14,360
Number 3, Tarum!

168
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:17,100
It's official! First place, Tanihayate!

169
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,740
We did it!

170
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:20,320
It's come in!

171
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:23,060
Ryo-san, it's a win bet,
so it pays fifty times!

172
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:24,420
Fifty times?

173
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:26,620
That's 25 million!

174
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:32,840
Come on, Ryo-san, let's head home
early today and celebrate in Ginza!

175
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:37,000
Right, when you're ahead,
knowing when to quit is what matters!

176
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:39,800
In the next race, I'll turn our
25 million into 100 million yen!

177
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:45,280
The next main race is a sure thing with 2-4.

178
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:47,860
It's the favorite,
but it should still pay four or five times.

179
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:49,840
We'll definitely reach the 100 million mark.

180
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,560
100 million!

181
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:52,060
W-what?

182
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:55,380
No. Damn it.

183
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:02,434
Ryo-san,

184
00:12:02,484 --> 00:12:05,080
So you're buying it after all?

185
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,440
No, my greed just

186
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:10,680
I'm taking this money home.

187
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:16,080
As long as there's even a trace of a wicked thought in my heart about making a profit,
greed will take advantage of me.

188
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,660
If I throw away these wicked thoughts,
the greed should disappear.

189
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:23,100
But maybe I'll make money...

190
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:25,580
It's getting bigger.

191
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:31,260
I can't do it anymore.

192
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:34,560
Um...

193
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,560
I won't answer!

194
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,200
All 242.5 million yen!

195
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:40,560
Buzz!

196
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:40,880
Yes!

197
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:42,320
Ryo-san! Stop it!

198
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,580
Did you really spend a
fortune on horse racing?

199
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:48,357
Yes, according to a message from
a friend of a senior officer,

200
00:12:48,407 --> 00:12:50,420
he apparently bought 25 million yen's worth.

201
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:50,900
What?

202
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:55,800
There he is, over there!

203
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:59,380
He filed a foul claim, but lost by a nose...

204
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:02,760
He's being crushed by his own greed!

205
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:03,660
How pathetic.

206
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:06,800
100 million yen.

207
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:12,620
A face is the root of all trouble.

208
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,500
Good morning.

209
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,640
Ryo-chan, you've got bed head!

210
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,840
The top of your head is totally flat.

211
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,720
It really is.

212
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:33,600
After pulling an all-nighter,
you slept in a weird position for 30 hours.

213
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,420
That's why I got bed head.

214
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,940
Still, it's perfectly flat.

215
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,800
It makes me want to put something on it.

216
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,640
Mine's really flat too, isn't it?

217
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,300
You're right.

218
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,800
It's super stable.

219
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,360
People often talk about
a flat back of the head,

220
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,840
but Ryo-chan, your crown is a sheer cliff.

221
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:58,540
It landed.

222
00:13:58,540 --> 00:13:59,700
More, more, put more on!

223
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,060
I wonder about this one.

224
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:02,520
It landed.

225
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:04,020
How about this one?

226
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:11,240
It landed, it landed!

227
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:18,940
M-my head is being used as

228
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:20,220
a playground!

229
00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:23,840
Well, this is a problem.

230
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:28,400
I have to attend my childhood friend's
wedding reception this afternoon.

231
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:31,040
It's fine, leave it to me.

232
00:14:32,980 --> 00:14:34,320
Okay, then all we need to do is

233
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,740
force it into place with some setting spray.

234
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,020
There, all done.

235
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,760
His bed-head is fixed.

236
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,420
Yeah, this is how it should be.
I feel much more settled.

237
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,680
He's back to normal, Reiko.

238
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:48,900
It's no good.

239
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:51,720
Store-bought set lotion
doesn't seem to be up to the job.

240
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:54,160
Guess I'll just go out like this.

241
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,000
An honorable responsibility.

242
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,320
Showing up with bed-head would be rude.

243
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:59,520
Wait a moment, please.

244
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:01,880
I'll go consult with them.

245
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:12,200
I've never seen a tuft this stubborn before.
It's hard to believe it's human hair.

246
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:15,860
A blow-dryer alone won't fix it.
Yeah, I figured as much.

247
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:18,520
Now then.

248
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:28,100
Okay.

249
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,320
Ready, go!

250
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,240
No, no, Goi-chan!

251
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,860
Nakagawa: Who on earth is that woman?

252
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:41,480
Yoko-san also handles special
makeup for Hollywood films.

253
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,740
She's a top-class hair and makeup artist.

254
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:45,360
Nice to meet you.

255
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,940
Special makeup.

256
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:51,000
I have to fly to LA
right after this today too.

257
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:55,500
There's a special makeup spray we
use that isn't sold commercially.

258
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,860
First, spray A on it.

259
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:01,060
then smooth your hair
into shape with a brush.

260
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,620
Then, when you spray B,

261
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,780
see? It's completely set.

262
00:16:05,780 --> 00:16:07,240
It's fixed!

263
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,440
Just like a pro.

264
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:11,360
With this, you should be able
to style it yourself easily.

265
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:14,180
You should've been
using this from the start.

266
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:17,160
Thanks, really. You saved me.

267
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:21,480
Spray A to set it,
and B is the one that hardens it, got it?

268
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:22,800
Got it. Thanks.

269
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:24,160
Well, I'm off then.

270
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:32,200
Ryo-chan, if you're going to the wedding,
shall I give you a side part?

271
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,360
Can you really do that?

272
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:36,020
Yeah. Now I'll set it with B.

273
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,220
It's done. How does it look, Ryo-chan?

274
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:41,280
It really is a side part.

275
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,780
It suits you pretty well, senpai.

276
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:45,600
That spray really is amazing.

277
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:50,300
I'd given up on any hairstyle except the crew cut,
after all.

278
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:53,020
Like this, I'm quite the handsome devil.

279
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,540
Thanks to attending the wedding reception,

280
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:59,100
apparently many new couples
get together there too,

281
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:01,060
so you should do your best too, senpai.

282
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:02,580
I see.

283
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:03,400
Alright.

284
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:07,180
I'll go research more hairstyles.

285
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:11,280
Maybe this will be the moment
Ryo-chan wakes up to fashion.

286
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:12,820
That's a good trend.

287
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:18,480
Hey, it's like Tamori from back in the day.
This is fun too.

288
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:22,580
No, it's childish. Let's do more.

289
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:36,000
Senpai, yeah, you're messing around with that spray...
Senpai's face! Senpai, what happened?

290
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:39,120
This is bad, it's hardened!

291
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,380
It's a natural style, it doesn't look weird.

292
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:45,640
No, it's my face. My face has hardened.

293
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,460
No way.

294
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:48,340
It's true.

295
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:52,860
I tried all sorts of things, but in the end
I figured I'd set it in the original style.

296
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:54,760
While I was spraying the B spray,

297
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,460
I realized I hadn't prepared a bag,

298
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,660
and just as I had that thought,
it accidentally got on my face.

299
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:02,780
And it hardened like this.

300
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:05,920
Of all things,
it didn't have to harden in that face.

301
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,580
Shouldn't you just spray
the A spray to put it back?

302
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:13,200
But I used too much,
and the A one ran out first.

303
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:16,080
Really, it won't move at all.

304
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:18,580
What are we going to do about the wedding?

305
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:22,180
Don't worry,
I'm sure she'll be back by then.

306
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:22,940
Excuse me.

307
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:23,540
Yes?

308
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,280
I'd like to ask for directions.

309
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:27,040
Yes, yes, miss. Where would you like to go?

310
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:27,820
No.

311
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:30,920
No, I'm not angry, it's just that...

312
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:33,500
Even if you say that...

313
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:36,480
Nakagawa, call that hairdresser back!

314
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,820
I'm calling her now.

315
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:41,100
Even knowing it's all stiffened up...

316
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,720
That face is scary.

317
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:46,400
Senpai, I'm sorry.

318
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,760
She's already left for LA,
and it goes straight to voicemail.

319
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:53,760
Okay, this should make
him a little less scary.

320
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:54,540
Really?

321
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:56,200
And the red smudged around the mouth, too...

322
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:58,720
If we make it look like he's in the middle of eating,
it'll look natural.

323
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,880
Uuugh...

324
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:08,140
Give him a microphone and an iron club,
and he's a demon with a club!

325
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:11,040
How about false eyelashes, too?

326
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:13,760
The more we do...

327
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:16,460
the more incomprehensibly scary he gets.

328
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:18,720
Stop playing with people's faces!

329
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:21,720
Damn, it's already time!

330
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,040
You're really going out like that?

331
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:28,160
I've been asked to give the speech
as the friend's representative.

332
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:30,500
I can't not go, can I?

333
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:33,580
Hey, couldn't this let
you change your expression?

334
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:35,200
Scotch tape

335
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:42,620
Takabo from the liquor shop has grown up nicely,
hasn't he.

336
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:45,280
He got himself a beautiful bride.

337
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:49,200
Anyway, what's going on with
the underside of that hairdo?

338
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:51,300
Seriously, Kankichin.

339
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:54,260
There are all sorts of
circumstances behind this.

340
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:57,520
But swallowing it without
chewing is so tough.

341
00:19:58,580 --> 00:20:03,520
Ugh, it finally went in.
It's rough, but it'd be a waste to leave it.

342
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:05,760
Ngh, so hard, so hard.

343
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:09,860
Finally got it down.

344
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,860
Can't I eat this some easier way?

345
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:20,140
Kankichi, you too, it's time you get a wife.

346
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:20,940
Ugh, no.

347
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:24,100
Hey, what's with that
attitude toward your father?

348
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,760
If you've got a complaint, say it.

349
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,640
Nothing.

350
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,920
Oh no, the tape peeled off.

351
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:30,840
Hey, hold on.

352
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:35,240
We've got to make it last until the speech.

353
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:39,380
He's come out making a weird face again.

354
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:41,300
Would you like some wine?

355
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,000
Sorry about that.

356
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,860
How about you, sir? Would you like some?

357
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,460
I think I'll take some.

358
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:47,520
Certainly.

359
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:50,860
Thanks, I appreciate it.

360
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:53,780
Thanks.

361
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,040
I'm terribly sorry.

362
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:00,220
It came off again.

363
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,680
This cellophane tape
really does peel off easily.

364
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,180
That startled me.

365
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:10,200
Why are you startling yourself?

366
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:13,420
We'd better get your face done quickly,
or it'll be time for your speech!

367
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:21,320
And now, the newlyweds, who have finished
changing outfits, will make their entrance.

368
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,220
Looks like we'll make it in time, somehow.

369
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:24,720
Did it turn out okay?

370
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:26,500
Your tie's crooked.

371
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:26,940
Mm.

372
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:29,520
Ah, it's dazzling!

373
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:39,480
Aaaaaaaah! Oh no, it's peeling off again!

374
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,040
What's wrong?

375
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:43,220
Hey! You!

376
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:44,040
Takabō!

377
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:44,880
Whoa!

378
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:46,860
It's me, Kankichi!

379
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:50,100
Kan-chan?! Why are you so angry?

380
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:52,500
I'm not angry at all, ahahaha!

381
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:54,440
Look, smile, damn it!

382
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:56,620
No matter how you look at it,
that face is angry!

383
00:21:56,860 --> 00:22:00,040
My face may look angry,
but in my heart I'm blessing you!

384
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:03,980
Mrs. Takabō,
congratulations on your wedding!

385
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:05,420
Th-thank you.

386
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:06,660
Waaah!

387
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:09,800
You idiot!

388
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:13,620
What the hell are you doing!

389
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:18,780
Just because you can't get a wife, you're wrecking other people's wedding?
You rotten, good-for-nothing punk!

390
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:22,660
I already told you I didn't mean it,
you goddamn old man!

391
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:28,500
Damn you, you actually did it. Raising your hand against your own parent,
you're pretty good at that, aren't you!

392
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:29,240
Parent, my ass!

393
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:31,060
Act like a parent!

394
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:32,920
Knock it off, you two!

395
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,840
Our cake!

396
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:44,980
Senpai! Senpai!
There was still a little A spray left!

397
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:46,000
What?

398
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:49,900
Really?

399
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,640
There was just a little bit left.

400
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,640
Good for you, Ryo-chan.

401
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,041
Alright,

402
00:22:55,091 --> 00:22:59,000
It came out perfect! All that's
left is to set it with this B spray.

403
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,740
Don't you need to set it anymore?

404
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:03,160
What are you talking about?
We got it looking this good.

405
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:06,420
If we set it with this, it won't get
bedhead for two or three days, right?

406
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:10,720
Nail the speech too,
and I'll be back in good standing.

407
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:15,380
Set the back of the head and the crown really well,
and the front too.

408
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:18,580
Senpai!

409
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:21,460
This is a problem.
I accidentally swallowed some spray.

410
00:23:24,260 --> 00:23:28,260
The groom and I were childhood
friends back in elementary school,

411
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:30,980
studying and playing sports together.

412
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:33,280
We got into fights sometimes, too,

413
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:36,640
but unlike me, he was an excellent student,

414
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:41,360
and I always got to copy
his notes for my homework.

415
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:45,620
Thanks to that, I graduated elementary
school without being held back.

416
00:23:45,620 --> 00:23:47,900
That's a face that doesn't show any of the four emotions,
is it not?

417
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:50,900
He doesn't even realize it,
which makes it even more pathetic.

418
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:53,840
Today, as a proper member of society,

419
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:57,560
I receive tremendous
respect from ordinary people,

420
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,600
and that is truly thanks to
him working behind the scenes.

421
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,000
Thank you, Takabō.

422
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:23,880
Surprise and commotion, timing and resolution,
quick and settled at the final tally.

423
00:24:53,880 --> 00:25:03,280
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, drawing the universe,
standing on the ground, the star of Kameari is coming, just as it should be.

424
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:08,660
"This should be fine, right?
" "As if it's fine!"

